target/
build/
.dart_tool/
node_modules/
.DS_Store

# `cargo llvm-cov` raw profiles. Most land under `target/`, but `duet-derive` is
# a **proc-macro** crate: its instrumented dylib is loaded by `rustc` itself
# while compiling every crate that derives, and those `rustc` processes run with
# the package directory as their working directory. So `crates/duet/*.profraw`
# and friends appear as soon as coverage runs, outside `target/` entirely.
*.profraw
*.profdata

# `packages/duet-js` build output. `src/` is the source of truth and Node runs
# it directly via type stripping, so `dist/` is only ever what `npm run build`
# just produced — committing it would create a second copy that can go stale.
# Nothing in this repository `include_str!`s or imports it; see the
# "This is not the client a real app uses" note on `BOOTSTRAP_HTML` in
# crates/duet-webview/src/bootstrap.rs for why the webview bootstrap is not
# built from it.
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Phase 0 spike fixture — regenerate with:
#   flutter create --platforms=macos --project-name spike_app spikes/spike_app
#   (cd spikes/spike_app && flutter build macos --debug)
spikes/spike_app/
# ...except the hand-edited entrypoint. Spikes B and C add a platform channel,
# a post-frame reporter, and the kReloadMarker const that hot reload mutates.
# `flutter create` will NOT regenerate these, so the file is tracked explicitly.
!spikes/spike_app/lib/
!spikes/spike_app/lib/main.dart
spikes/*/target/

# Phase 2b-6 Flutter guest fixture — regenerate scaffolding (macos/, .idea/,
# pubspec.lock, ...) with:
#   flutter create --platforms=macos --org com.example --project-name duet_guest fixtures/duet_guest
#
# `/*` rather than `/`: git cannot re-include anything inside an excluded
# *directory*, so `fixtures/duet_guest/` made the `!` lines below dead letters —
# every hand-written file under it had to be forced in with `git add -f`, and a
# new one was silently skipped instead. Excluding the directory's *children*
# leaves the negations able to do their job.
fixtures/duet_guest/*
# ...except the hand-written app: the guest drivers, their tests, the manifests,
# and this fixture's own README. `flutter create` will NOT regenerate these, so
# they are tracked explicitly.
#
# `pubspec_overrides.yaml` is tracked too, and must be: it is what points this
# fixture at `packages/duet` and `packages/duet_flutter` in THIS checkout rather
# than at whatever is on pub.dev. The three macOS examples are the only
# end-to-end proof that the Dart packages and the Rust host still agree, so they
# have to run against the working tree.
!fixtures/duet_guest/lib/
!fixtures/duet_guest/test/
!fixtures/duet_guest/pubspec.yaml
!fixtures/duet_guest/pubspec_overrides.yaml
!fixtures/duet_guest/README.md
